edition 5;

module ml.spec;

// What `ml` says about itself: the flag table that drives the parser, `introspect` and `skill` (cancho docs/agent-toolbox.md
// D11), the rules of its own beside the shared catalogue, and the log records. Three tables, each written once; the schemas
// (scripts/schemas.py), the fixtures (tests/fixtures/cli.json) and the gates (tests/conformance/test_tables.py) are checked
// against them, so a flag, a rule or a log record that is in one place and not in the others fails the build.
//
// Format: entries separated by `;`, fields by `|`, so no help text holds either character.

import toolbox.describe;

// name|short|kind|role|default|help
pub fn flag_table() -> [] &static [byte] {
    return "root||path|root||resolve FILE, --model-file, --output and --log beneath this directory, following no symbolic link, and refuse paths outside it;model||choice:constant|none|constant|the model fit builds. Only constant is built: for a regression the training mean, for a classification the majority class and its probability. No other model name is accepted;task||choice:regression/classification|none|regression|what the target column is: a number to predict (regression) or a label with exactly two values (classification);target||text|none||fit: the name of the column to predict, as the header spells it;drop||text|none||columns to ignore, header names separated by commas (fit, predict, eval). A dropped column is not part of the stored schema;output||path|path-write||fit: where to write the model file. The directory must exist. An existing file is refused unless --overwrite;model-file||path|path-read||predict, eval: the model file to read;overwrite||bool|guard||fit: replace an existing --output. The new file is written beside it under a temporary name and renamed over it, so a reader never sees half a file;dry-run||bool|guard||fit: read, check and fit, then report what would be written (planned_actions) and exit 9, writing nothing;limit||nat|none|1000|predict: the most rows in one page of predictions, at least 1;from||nat|none|0|predict: the row to start the page at, counting data rows from 0;max-rows||nat|none|10000000|the most data rows read. More is ml.input.too-many-rows;max-columns||nat|none|4096|the most columns read. More is ml.input.too-many-columns;max-cells||nat|none|400000000|the most rows times columns. More is ml.input.too-many-cells;max-line-bytes||nat|none|1048576|the longest line read. A longer one is limit.line-too-long;max-bytes||nat|none|16777216|predict, eval: the largest model file read. A larger one is limit.input-too-large;log||path|path-write||append NDJSON records of this run to this file. Records hold counts, rule tags and hashes, never a cell, a column name or a path;log-max-bytes||nat|none|1048576|refuse to log into a file already this long (limit.log-full). The log of one run adds at most 2048 bytes;format||choice:json/text|none|json|json: one document on one line. text: a few lines for a person, errors as sentences on standard error";
}

// tag|exit|repairable|summary. The shared catalogue (toolbox.rules) has args.*, path.*, io.*, limit.line-too-long,
// limit.input-too-large, conflict.exists and path.bad-name; these are ml's own. Summaries end `Hint: ... Repair: ...`.
pub fn extra() -> [] &static [byte] {
    return "args.unknown-command|2|never|the first operand is not fit, predict or eval. Hint: the verbs are fit, predict and eval, and ml introspect and ml skill describe them. Repair: none.;ml.param.out-of-range|2|never|a numeric flag is below its minimum or above its ceiling. Hint: the range is in detail and in introspect limits. Repair: none.;ml.input.empty|8|never|the file has a header and no data rows. Hint: give a file with at least one data row. Repair: none.;ml.input.too-many-rows|8|never|more data rows than --max-rows. Hint: raise --max-rows up to its ceiling, or fit on a sample of the rows. Repair: none.;ml.input.too-many-columns|8|never|more columns than --max-columns. Hint: raise --max-columns up to its ceiling, or drop columns with --drop. Repair: none.;ml.input.too-many-cells|8|never|rows times columns is more than --max-cells. Hint: raise --max-cells up to its ceiling, or use fewer rows or columns. Repair: none.;ml.input.non-numeric|8|sometimes|a cell of a kept column is not an integer or a decimal, or is empty. The line, the column and the reason are in detail. Hint: drop the column with --drop, or fix the cell. Repair: retry.;ml.input.non-finite|8|never|a cell is nan or inf. Hint: remove the row or the column. Repair: none.;ml.input.unsupported-type|8|never|a cell is a number this slice cannot read exactly: it has an exponent, or the column needs more than 12 digits. Floating-point text needs the cancho-table float reader, which is not merged. Hint: scale the column to an integer or a short decimal, or drop it with --drop. Repair: none.;ml.input.unsupported-csv|8|never|the file has a double quote. Quoted CSV fields are not read in this slice. Hint: remove the quotes, or use a different delimiter-free export. Repair: none.;ml.input.duplicate-column|8|never|two columns have the same header name, or a column name is empty. Hint: rename the columns in the file. Repair: none.;ml.input.unknown-column|3|never|--target or --drop names a column that is not in the header. Hint: names are compared exactly, byte for byte. Repair: none.;parse.csv-ragged-row|8|never|a data row has a different number of fields from the header. The line is in detail. Hint: fix the row. Repair: none.;ml.label.single-class|8|never|a classification target has one value. Hint: a model needs both classes in the training rows. Repair: none.;ml.label.not-binary|8|never|a classification target has more than two values. Hint: only two-class targets are built. Repair: none.;ml.label.not-integer|8|never|a classification target is not an integer column. Hint: label the classes with integers. Repair: none.;ml.schema.mismatch|8|sometimes|the input columns differ from the fitted schema: missing, extra or of another type. They are named in detail. Hint: the missing columns must be added. Extra columns can be ignored with --drop. Repair: retry.;ml.model.bad-magic|8|never|the file does not start with CML1. Hint: this is not a cancho-ml model file. Repair: none.;ml.model.version|8|never|the file has a format version this reader does not know. Hint: refit with this version of ml. Repair: none.;ml.model.truncated|8|never|the file ends before the end the header and the section lengths promise, or a length runs past the end. Hint: copy the file again. Repair: none.;ml.model.checksum|8|never|the SHA-256 at the end of the file is not the hash of the bytes before it. Hint: the file changed after it was written. Repair: none.;ml.model.malformed|8|never|the file passes the checksum but a section is not what the format allows. The section is in detail. Hint: refit. Repair: none.;limit.log-full|8|never|the --log file is already --log-max-bytes long. Hint: move the log away, or raise --log-max-bytes. Repair: none.";
}

// the rules ml can emit: the shared ones it reaches, then its own (extra)
pub fn rules() -> [] &static [byte] {
    return "args.unknown-flag;args.missing-value;args.bad-value;args.unexpected-value;args.duplicate-flag;args.conflict;args.missing-operand;args.required-flag;args.too-many-operands;args.unknown-command;path.empty;path.dotdot;path.absolute;path.outside-root;path.too-long;path.symlink;path.bad-name;io.not-found;io.not-a-directory;io.is-a-directory;io.permission-denied;io.read-failed;io.write-failed;conflict.exists;limit.line-too-long;limit.input-too-large;limit.log-full;ml.param.out-of-range;ml.input.empty;ml.input.too-many-rows;ml.input.too-many-columns;ml.input.too-many-cells;ml.input.non-numeric;ml.input.non-finite;ml.input.unsupported-type;ml.input.unsupported-csv;ml.input.duplicate-column;ml.input.unknown-column;parse.csv-ragged-row;ml.label.single-class;ml.label.not-binary;ml.label.not-integer;ml.schema.mismatch;ml.model.bad-magic;ml.model.version;ml.model.truncated;ml.model.checksum;ml.model.malformed";
}

// the flags each verb takes, comma separated. A flag of the table that a verb does not list is args.conflict with that verb;
// every flag of the table is listed by at least one verb (tests/conformance/test_tables.py).
pub fn allowed(verb: int) -> [] &static [byte] {
    if verb == 1 {
        return "root,model,task,target,drop,output,overwrite,dry-run,max-rows,max-columns,max-cells,max-line-bytes,log,log-max-bytes,format";
    }
    if verb == 2 {
        return "root,model-file,drop,limit,from,max-rows,max-columns,max-cells,max-line-bytes,max-bytes,log,log-max-bytes,format";
    }
    return "root,model-file,drop,max-rows,max-columns,max-cells,max-line-bytes,max-bytes,log,log-max-bytes,format";
}

// event|fields. The records of the NDJSON log (--log). Each is one line, a closed object; a field is a count, a flag, a
// rule tag or a hash, never data. `seq` is the position in the run.
pub fn log_table() -> [] &static [byte] {
    return "start|event,seq,command,version;read|event,seq,rows,columns,bytes;write|event,seq,bytes,sha256;end|event,seq,ok,exit,rule";
}

// name|default|ceiling
pub fn limits() -> [] &static [byte] {
    return "limit|1000|1000000;from|0|1000000000;max-rows|10000000|1000000000;max-columns|4096|8192;max-cells|400000000|1099511627776;max-line-bytes|1048576|16777216;max-bytes|16777216|268435456;log-max-bytes|1048576|1073741824";
}

pub fn tool() -> [] describe.Tool {
    return describe.Tool { name: "ml", version: "0.1.0", summary: "Fit, apply and score a model on a CSV file, with the refusals of a tool an agent can read. One model is built, honestly: constant. For a regression it predicts the training mean, for a classification the majority class and its probability. fit reads a CSV (integer and short-decimal columns), writes a model file (CML1: sections, tensor records, a SHA-256 trailer), predict applies the stored schema and model to another CSV, eval scores a model on a CSV: accuracy from exact counts, or the sum of squared errors as an exact decimal and the RMSE from it in three IEEE steps. The same input gives the same model bytes. Every refusal is a rule tag with its hint. Verbs: fit FILE (--target, --output; --task, --drop, --overwrite, --dry-run), predict FILE (--model-file; --drop, --limit, --from), eval FILE (--model-file; --drop). The first operand is the verb, the second the CSV file. Floating-point text is refused (ml.input.unsupported-type) until cancho-table's float reader is merged.", usage: "fit:     ml [--root DIR] [--task regression|classification] --target NAME --output MODEL [--drop NAMES] [--overwrite] [--dry-run] [--max-rows N] [--max-columns N] [--max-cells N] [--max-line-bytes N] [--log FILE] [--format json|text] fit FILE\npredict: ml [--root DIR] --model-file MODEL [--drop NAMES] [--limit N] [--from N] [--max-bytes N] [--log FILE] [--format json|text] predict FILE\neval:    ml [--root DIR] --model-file MODEL [--drop NAMES] [--max-bytes N] [--log FILE] [--format json|text] eval FILE\n\nFILE: a CSV with a header row, comma separated, no quotes. Cells are integers or decimals of at most 12 digits. Paths are relative to --root when given.", output: "document", schema: "ml.v1", flags: flag_table(), operands: "VERB|none|1|1|fit, predict or eval;FILE|path-read|1|1|the CSV file to read, a path relative to --root when given (absolute paths, .. and symbolic links are refused), whose first row is the header", rules: rules(), extra_rules: extra(), limits: limits(), reversibility: "irreversible-bounded", stdin: "no", guarantees: "deterministic;idempotent;dry_run" };
}
